      "content": "8. Dispersion of Light"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Myopia (near-sightedness) is corrected using concave lenses, while Hypermetropia (far-sightedness) requires convex lenses.",
        "Convex mirrors are used as rear-view mirrors in automobiles because they produce an erect and diminished image with a wider field of view.",
        "Total Internal Reflection (TIR) is frequently tested and is the core principle behind optical fibers and mirages."
      ],
      "id": "rb21rju"
